    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "PRIOR-ART",
      "narration_text": "What have other people done? Checkers like axe, Lighthouse and WAVE find problems, but a developer still has to fix them. Overlay widgets promise one-line compliance. In twenty twenty-five the F T C ordered accessiBe to pay one million dollars over exactly that claim. Researchers have shown language models can repair violations. One system, AccessGuru, reduced violation scores by up to eighty-four percent. What none of them give a small team is the whole path: fix the source, prove it, and let a person decide.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
