    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "LOOP",
      "narration_text": "Now, how I'll build it. A-eleven-Y Proof runs a loop. Observe: load the page in a real browser and run axe core. Decide: pick one violation. Act: patch the code in a sandbox. Record: write every step to a ledger. That ledger is its memory, so it never retries a fix a person already refused. And stop, when the re-scan is clean, when it hits its budget of steps and dollars, or when it refuses. Never just because the model says it's done.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
