    {
      "beat_id": "B13",
      "act": "MEASURE",
      "narration_text": "How will I know it worked? I split the test cases before tuning anything: a development set to build against, and a held-out set I don't touch until the end. On held-out pages it passes if at least eighty percent of violations are fixed, with zero new violations and zero broken layouts, checked by axe and screenshot diffs, not by the model. And on real repositories, maintainers have to accept at least seven of ten pull requests.",
